From 85123c2e0d27597fc5a688068d654d88bb3fd5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:08:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Fence delta-base persistence across async writes and
 quit

Problem: review 5899205930 reproduced quit losing an in-flight copy,
delete being undone by a captured async writer, and quit-only stores
exceeding the 48 MiB disk budget.

Why: flush cleared dirty keys before awaiting filesystem work; quit
could no longer see them. Async publication did not revalidate ownership
after writing. The synchronous path omitted eviction entirely.
Root (happened): async and terminal writers had no shared publication
invariant. Keep dirty ownership until publication, serialize async
flushes, fence on current copy and quit epoch, and use distinct temps.
Use explicit delete intents so memory eviction does not delete disk bases.
Both paths enforce the same budget, including interrupted temp files.
Root (not caught): tests covered idle quit and deletion after completed
flushes, not deterministic in-flight barriers or repeated quit-only stores.
Recurrence: prior review fixed hot-base LRU and write amplification, not
these lifecycle boundaries. No protocol or eligibility changes.

Proof: new barrier and repeated-reopen tests fail in all three reported
ways on b7a1298be4. After repair, 78 tests pass across delta-reads,
delta-persistence-lifecycle, json-fetch and slow-link. Typecheck passes
(with shared worktree dependency link); eslint and scripts/check 20/20
pass. Live Desktop restart and hub-roll proof remain pending deployment.
